From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 02:28:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: Never let a G16 lane head lap an unretired flight

reserve_flight() bounds a lane's new entries against the firmware read
and done cursors, but not against flights that the firmware has consumed
and the driver has not yet retired. retire() checks each flight's ring
head with a modular comparison that is only unambiguous within half the
0x500-entry ring. A burst of hundreds of small Works can therefore move
the cursors more than 640 entries past an unretired flight's head, after
which its ring check is false forever and it never retires.

Apply the same bound the channel epochs already have: refuse (as
workqueue backpressure) while the new head would be half a ring past any
unretired flight on the lane.

Signed-off-by: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 7b6371a616f86469ea8b3c24f5d538c2dc900433)
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_runtime.rs | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_runtime.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_runtime.rs
index 9364faeef3ca..6ce7a5abb3a5 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_runtime.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_runtime.rs
@@ -582,6 +582,20 @@ fn reserve_flight(
                     self.report_pressure(16, "workqueue");
                     return Err(EBUSY);
                 }
+                // Retirement compares the firmware cursors with each flight's
+                // head modulo the ring, which is only unambiguous within half
+                // a ring. Like the channel epochs above, never let the head
+                // run half a ring past an unretired flight on this lane, or
+                // that flight's ring check stays false and it never retires.
+                let next = (lane.head + entries[stage]) % 0x500;
+                if self.flights.iter().any(|f| {
+                    f.queues
+                        .iter()
+                        .any(|&(pointers, head)| pointers == lane.pointers && !reached(next, head, 0x500))
+                }) {
+                    self.report_pressure(16, "workqueue");
+                    return Err(EBUSY);
+                }
             }
         }
         drop(guard);
